---
title: Garlic Shrimp With Smoked Paprika
servings: 4
cuisine: spanish
main_protein: seafood
prep_time: "15 minutes"
cook_time: "15 minutes"
tags:
  - dinner
prep:
  - Thaw, peel and devein the shrimp
  - Pat shrimp dry with a paper towel
  - Thinly slice 2 large garlic cloves
---
Pat @large shrimp{36}, thawed, peeled + deveined, dry with a paper towel and place them in a small bowl. Toss them in 1 Tbsp of the @olive oil{3%tbsp} and a bit of @salt{} + @black pepper{}.

Heat up a #frying pan{} or skillet over medium-high heat. Once the pan is hot (a splash of water should sizzle on it), place the shrimp on the pan. They should be in a single layer with a bit of space between each piece – you may need to do this in stages, depending on size of pan.

Cook the shrimp for ~{1%minute} per side, then remove and set aside in a bowl. They'll be opaque, pink, and slightly browned when done.

In the same pan, add remaining 2 Tbsp olive oil and @garlic{2%cloves}, thinly sliced. Sauté garlic for ~{1%minute}, until browned and slightly fragrant. Stir in @smoked paprika{1.5%tsp} and @honey{1%tsp}, then add cooked shrimp back into the pan. Toss to coat.

Remove pan from heat and serve shrimp immediately. Season with salt + pepper, as desired.
